> **Farzana says:**
>
> I always recommend buying loose first. Not because it saves money — though it often does — but because you actually know what you are buying. When a stone is already set, you are trusting someone else picked well. When you read the certificate yourself, you picked well.

## Lab-Grown Loose Radiant Cut Diamond Prices by Carat

Lab-grown radiant cut diamonds are IGI-certified at the entry level, with GIA lab certifications available at a higher price point. Proportions matter just as much for lab-grown stones — a lab radiant at 73% depth underperforms the same way a natural radiant does.

### 1 Carat Lab-Grown Radiant Cut Diamond

The 1ct lab radiant entry is [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for an E-VVS1 IGI — a top-tier grade at under $1,000, a combination that does not exist in natural diamonds.

| Stone | Grade | Price | What this means |
